<!--/Post: 4665-->
<!--Post: 4666--><!--Time: 1106649209-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4666"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 2:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Actually, I&#39;ve since learned there is a small portion still missing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4666-->
<!--Post: 4667--><!--Time: 1106652934-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4667"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 3:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very cool. <BR>Thank you Tom<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4667-->
<!--Post: 4682--><!--Time: 1106671399-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4682"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 8:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My initial insight into the reveal tends to make me think that there is meaning to the victims&#39; bodies being faced in certain directions.  I think that there would be many other items of special interest that BTK could have mentioned to the police about the crime scene besides body positions in relation to N/S/E/W.  One thing that I might want to add, is the importance of NSEW. In Wichita direction giving, compared to other places I&#39;ve lived in the world,  everything here is relative to NSEW, when you ask for directions to an unknown location.  As a newcomer to the area, I would ask directions, and be suprised at the locals giving me &#34;it&#39;s on the South side of &#40;insert landmark&#41;&#34; as acceptable directions.  My own girlfriend has lived here all 21 years of her life, and she can&#39;t tell me what the road names are that connect to each other to get somewhere!  She just knows to head East on this road, then South at this intersection, &#34;I don&#39;t know, I&#39;d have to show you!&#34;; that kind of thing.  So back to the relevance to BTK&#39;s Otero letter, I think that he would have lived in the area long enough to develop that line of thought, and perhaps if he is involved in the airline industry, &#40;pilot, etc.&#41; then the directions would be second nature in describing, and are valid insights into his psyche and reasoning.  This could point to BTK being from the South, and on the East coast for example.  Or even living in the Southeast part of Wichita.  IMO, the fact that they are all positioned certain ways, in certain areas of the house, and in certain &#34;face up, face down&#34; positions or hanging, is quite significant.  If you think in dimensional aspects, there could be a model forming some symbol or sign.  I just don&#39;t think it is coincidental.  We&#39;d have to have a blueprint or 3D landcad of the house, and exact body positions in relation to the model.  Anyone think they could guesswork this into something we can start with? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4682-->
<!--Post: 4683--><!--Time: 1106672184-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4683"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 8:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Tom<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4683-->
<!--Post: 4685--><!--Time: 1106677033-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4685"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 10:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very interesting. Almost looks as if it was written by someone who viewed the scene, not someone who actually committed the murders; with perhaps the one exception which seems very strange to me: <BR> <BR>Slip knotts on Joe and Joseph neck to hold leg down <BR>or was at one time ?? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4685-->
<!--Post: 4686--><!--Time: 1106677341-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4686"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 10:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My intial reaction to the full otero letter was this guy is a cop. The descriptions he gives are much like notes a police officer writes in a police report. However, after reading it more carefully and thinking it over, I believe that BTK is writing this way because he is writing to the police. I think he writing it that way because I think BTK wishs he could be a cop. He probably tried to be a cop. He probably tried to be alot of things but could never fit in.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4686-->
<!--Post: 4692--><!--Time: 1106683051-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4692"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 11:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Tom. <BR> <BR>He makes good distinctions about the TYPES of ropes, and seems to know rope-related hardware &#40;i.e., clove-hitch&#41;.   <BR> <BR>Even if he yanked these cords/ropes from their proper place at the Otero house, he still seems a bit too knowledgeable.   <BR> <BR>---Hemp rope: ¼ diameter &#40;He knows the exact diameter?&#41; <BR>---Clothesline cord with clove-hitch &#40;Nice hardware vocabulary&#41; <BR>---Window blind cord <BR> <BR>If English is not BTK’s first language, he still knows related buzzwords &amp; phrases: <BR>--Crosswise <BR>--All one length <BR>--Slip knots <BR> <BR>I wonder if he could be a building superintendent who ties up the recycle with hemp cord and slip knots; and who has hung window blinds and clothesline cord for the tenants.   <BR> <BR>And then I read  “Thermostat turn down.”   Does that mean HE turned down the thermostat?  I don’t think they had automatic set-back thermostats back then.  So either someone at the Otero house turned it down &#40;thinking they were about to leave the house for the day&#41; or BTK himself turned it down. <BR> <BR>If BTK turned it down, that also may be in keeping with superintendent duties.  Back in the fifties, I believe the superintendent monitored the thermostat for the building.  He held the key that locked a plastic casing that was over the thermostat. <BR> <BR>Plenty of occupations are related to rope &amp; related hardware, but for some reason, superintendent sticks in my mind.   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4692-->
<!--Post: 4697--><!--Time: 1106687082-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4697"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 1:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Turning the thermostat down throws off the time of death when bodies are left for long periods of time...don&#39;t know if that&#39;s why he did it or not and it didn&#39;t work...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4697-->
<!--Post: 4701--><!--Time: 1106689812-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4701"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 1:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;d be mildly surprised if he didn&#39;t try to become a police officer but failed. His rope knowledge could have come from the Boy Scouts, military, self-study or any other number of places. A wannabe, for sure. Thanks Tom, and I&#39;m glad WPD released this. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4701-->
<!--Post: 4720--><!--Time: 1106692255-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4720"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 2:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, they didn&#39;t release it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4720-->
<!--Post: 4723--><!--Time: 1106692851-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4723"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hmmm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hmmm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 2:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting comment on Joe with the wreck the week before.  Did he read of the wreck, or did he witness the wreck, was he in the wreck?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4723-->
<!--Post: 4727--><!--Time: 1106695114-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4727"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Biggles<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Biggles<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 3:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The comment on the rib injury from the wreck, plus the reference to &#34;Joe&#34; rather than Joseph &#40;or &#34;Jose&#34; as many newspaper reports of the time used&#41; suggests to me that either he was known to his victims, or to my mind more likely, he spent time talking with them after tying them. I could imagine him really enjoying the power of having them in his control and at the same time carrying on in a seemingly &#34;normal&#34; manner. <BR> <BR>Another thing that strikes me as interesting is that when listing the clothes of each victim, for each of the two females he includes socks but doesn&#39;t go into the same detail for the males. Perhaps this hints at a foot fetish of some kind?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4727-->
<!--Post: 4732--><!--Time: 1106699137-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4732"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 4:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom, <BR> <BR>Then who is your source?  BTK?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4732-->
<!--Post: 4733--><!--Time: 1106699176-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4733"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 4:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom - the letter - fascinating. <BR> <BR>Did you get in when you were in Wichita?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4733-->
<!--Post: 4743--><!--Time: 1106706205-->
