<!--Post: 4762--><!--Time: 1106723025-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4762"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 11:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Peculiar how all of us notice different things in the exact same letter. <BR> <BR>What knocked me on the noggin&#39; was BTK&#39;s obsession with direction.  On a quick skim, I count no less than &#42;nine&#42; references to direction/orientation.  This suggests to me that at least one &#40;maybe more&#41; of the following may be true: <BR> <BR>a&#41; BTK is meticulous... perhaps in an ocd type way, or in a mental sense &#40;has an incredible capacity for trivia or obsession with facts and details&#41;; <BR> <BR>b&#41; BTK arranged the crime scene intentionally to convey some sort of meaning or message &#40;for example, the &#34;peace sign&#34; rebtk suggests; <BR> <BR>c&#41; BTK works with directionality daily &#40;dispatcher?, aviator?, engineer? surveyor? other ideas any one?&#41;; <BR> <BR>d&#41; either BTK had been in the home many times and was intimately familiar with its layout or, as he composes the Otero letter, he is referring to a blueprint or floor plan of the Otero home or, perhaps, an aerial photograph of the neighborhood on which the Otero home was identifiable. <BR> <BR>I think either &#34;c&#34; or &#34;d&#34; &#42;must&#42; be true since he is describing directional orientations inside the home and even on different levels of the home.  Speaking as a guy only average at working with direction, but still manages to confuse his wife all the time with driving directions like &#34;turn south at the stop sign&#34;, I just can&#39;t conceive that BTK could describe the crime scene with all these directional details accurately without some sort of external reference or expertise in dealing with directions. Most especially if he entered the Otero home for the very first time that morning in the heat of a sexually-driven mayhem- who in this state would give the first thought to what direction the feet were pointing?!?  To me &#42;this&#42; is precisely the question. <BR> <BR>Tom, do you know if, in fact, there are any errors in BTK&#39;s descriptions of the Otero crime scene as regards objects/victims placements and directional orientations?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4762-->
<!--Post: 4766--><!--Time: 1106724702-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4766"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 11:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Speaking of &#34;face up,face down&#34; as Catcher mentions, do people think this newer information, with specifics of that type, validates the &#34;From BTK&#34; post about &#34;the faceupthe facedown&#34;?  Perhaps this was his way of offering validation.  Or is this information that a poser likely could have gotten?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4766-->
<!--Post: 4768--><!--Time: 1106727460-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4768"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 12:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Apparently the small portion that is missing contains a reference that BTK made to an event that happened in the house after he left. <BR> He would have known about this only from someone who was at the scene, police investigators, detectives, original police responders, dispatch, paramedics, coroners office or by monitoring police channels or through a relative of the Otero&#39;s who were told of the event or by a social worker who was sent to comfort the three surviving Otero children.  <BR>BTK somehow gained an insiders knowlege of the crime scene  by someone else other than himself. <BR> <BR>Icetejan noted some examples of phases used by BTK that shows he is very comfortable and knowlegable of the English language. Another example he uses in the letter is &#34;the radio was blaring.&#34; <BR> <BR>He may have taken pictures of the crime scene to help him remember everything in detail and I&#39;m sure he did but why did he not remember that the appliance in the basement next to Josephine&#39;s body was a clothes dryer or a freezer? <BR> <BR>Julie appears to be the primary target of sexual interest to him. she was the only one he strangled twice. He must have strangled her to near death then let her come back to life and then finished her off. <BR> <BR>Interestingly he spells garotte correctly when describing Joseph Otero&#39;s strangulation but spell it incorrectly as garote when thinking of a possible name to call himself. <BR> <BR>The car couldn&#39;t have been out of gas. To get to Dillion&#39;s parking lot from the Otero house he would have gone in a uphill grade and then crossed oncomming traffic to pull into parking lot. Doesn&#39;t sound like the actions of someone who has discovered that not only is the gas tank is emty but is pressing on the gas pedal and getting no response..<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4768-->
<!--Post: 4769--><!--Time: 1106729190-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4769"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 12:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Great comments and observations, all.  From what can be gleaned from this one old letter, I think release of his more recent writings would crack the case. <BR> <BR>If his posts here are not posers, then it would appear there has been a huge improvement in certain aspects of his writing - beyond things he might have been faking.  Recent writings would verify this, and could be readily linked to existing writings available to somebody somewhere.  Also, I think it might pin down what he&#39;s been doing for the last 20 years.  English instructor?  Journalist?  Something&#39;s gotta give if his writing has improved that much. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t take the line about &#34;Car was dirty inside, out of gas.&#34; as a lie.  It is clearly the reaction of a childless OCD to a &#34;family&#34; car.  An OCD will keep it immaculate with the tank topped off - anything below 1/4 tank is &#34;out of gas&#34;.  Anybody who was ever a parent knows how quickly such unrealistic standards go out the window.  I&#39;ve known OCDs who were cured just by parenthood.  Four or five kids means lots of love and not much order.  The obscenity of his comment is all the greater knowing he just destroyed what he probably could never understand.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4769-->
<!--Post: 4775--><!--Time: 1106740334-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4775"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 3:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->An element in the letter that stood out for me - is the mention that Josephine&#39;s glasses were in the same bedroom Joe was found dead in. <BR> <BR>That is bothersome because it indicates that the girl may have been in the room when her father died.  I suppose BTK could have placed them there later, however.   <BR> <BR>As far as the taxpayer thing - I see it as a reaffirmation of a possible Republican affiliation - no offense to all the GOP&#39;ers here.     <BR> <BR>One thing I did notice was that the mother was strangled twice - hard enough to bring blood to her face.  The others seem to have been killed quicker. <BR> <BR>I would be interested to find out if she, and possibly the other women killed by BTK had at one point insulted him - or spoke down to him in some matter.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4775-->
<!--Post: 4780--><!--Time: 1106749211-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4780"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lazysean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lazysean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 6:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno -- interesting.  I&#39;ve never heard that before &#40;btk having insider info&#41;.  I had been thinking the missing part of the letter might contain some reference to the story of Joseph being temporarily untied and forced to write something.  &#42;If&#42; that story were true, I can&#39;t imagine how else the investigators would have known it had happened unless BTK told them. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
