<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4814"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 10:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Armchairpi, <BR>Read my post above yours, I think we are looking at similar angles in regards to the letters.  I agree with your interpretation. <BR> <BR>Rebtk, <BR>I see you derived a peace sign, I did the same as I posted above, and got some symbol that looked similar to a peace sign, but not exactly.  It looks to me like BTK combined into one symbol/initial with the B not curved but diagonal points intersecting other lines.  I&#39;d have to draw it.  I hope Tom decides to release the BTK&#39;s symbol.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
