<!--Post: 4832--><!--Time: 1106768404-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4832"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 11:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;Strangulation once, then hung.&#34; Well, BTK is a liar, we know that from previous statements but if he&#39;s telling the truth here &#40;and he&#39;s trying to establish his bona fides with police, so I think it likely&#41; he strangled Josephine once, then hanged &#40;or &#34;hung,&#34; as BTK wrote&#41; her. Thought this might be the case. That Mrs. Otero received the most violence further underscores that she was probably the main focus of the attack. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
