<!--Post: 4937--><!--Time: 1106833659-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4937"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 5:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey yall, Look at how much detail is in the letter. Did he take notes at the scene? Photographic memory or pictues from scene? Now I know there are people who know what direction they are headed by instinct. But this is extreme. Did he have a compas? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
