<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5518"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 12:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I read somwhere that in BTK&#39;s detailed sketch of the Fox crime scene that the image of the bedroom wasn&#39;t from a perspective that one could have took with a camera. Instead it was drawn from the other side of the wall as if the wall was not there. Also the number of squares in the headboard were less than their really was. The lamp was slighty different and the shoes were in a different position than they really were.  <BR>So on this one it was like he was relying on memory and not copying the drawing from a photograph that he took.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5518-->
<!--Post: 5536--><!--Time: 1107180853-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5536"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 6:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I thought that it was a fact that BTK had taken photographs.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5536-->
<!--Post: 5561--><!--Time: 1107193607-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5561"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thacket3<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thacket3<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 9:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found the comment about the &#34;bruise&#34; being from a car wreck a few weeks earlier interesting.  So it would appear to me that he knew them on a &#34;friend&#34; or co-worker level.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5561-->
<!--Post: 5562--><!--Time: 1107194208-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5562"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 9:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Tom, for posting the letter. I found it incredibly difficult to read objectively because I kept thinking, My God, these are people.  There is not a sense of that at all in his writings.   <BR> <BR>What I fnd interesting, actually, is a line that was already released long ago from this letter. It&#39;s BTK&#39;s postscript which purports to state some &#39;factual&#39; information regarding the &#34;MO&#34; of killers such as he. I swear I can see him smirking as he wrote that - knowing full well he intended to change his and quite sucessfully. I have never thought that man who calls himself BTK stopped killing, rather he stopped killing as BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5562-->
<!--Post: 5595--><!--Time: 1107212627-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5595"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 3:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Blade, BTK did indeed take photgraphs but there are only three known photographs taken by him that were sent in the various communication. Those three of are various positions of the body of Vicki Wegerle. Police may have additional photographs and have not released that information to the public. <BR>BTK sent in a communication a hand drawn sketch of the Nancy Fox murder scene and he also sent in a communication a hand drawn sketch of the interior of Anna Williams&#39; home that he broke into. Due to slight inconsistancies with an accurate representation in these two sketches it was believed by some that BTK didn&#39;t draw them from looking at a photograph he had taken otherwise he would have sent a photograph in. Instead it is believed that BTK may have a photographic memory. <BR>The three Wegerle photos are the only known photographs of crime scenes in existance I think. <BR>Oher crime scenes like the Otero&#39;s he writes about them in detail as evidenced in the letter a the top of this thread but it was not accompanied by photographs or sketches. <BR> <BR>Thacket3, I don&#39;t think that BTK had to necessarily know of Otero&#39;s injury and car accident prior to the murders. BTK could have been binding his victims and Otero not thinking he was going to be killed asked BTK to be careful tying him up because he had an injury and then told BTK how he recieved the injury. BTK may have merely learned of it that day from Otero. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5595-->
</table></td></tr></table>
